+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The clinic publishes the same people the other way round. One page lists every specialty the clinic knows, each by its stored name, and under each specialty the veterinarians who hold it, named in full — first name then last name, as in Helen Leary `[REQ-VET-003]`. The page lists specialties, not the whole roster: a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it. Every specialty appears at once, with no paging. Reading is all the page offers; managing veterinarians or specialties stays out of scope (NG-2). The page is reachable only by its own address: no navigation entry and no other page links to it — whether it gains a visible entry point is an [open question](#open-questions).
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name on one page, with no paging.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each of them is shown by first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding more than one specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears under each specialty held.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty held by no veterinarian is still listed, with no veterinarian shown under it.
+2. A clinic that knows no specialties yields an empty page rather than a failure.
+3. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+4. A specialty name is shown as stored and is not translated. `REQ-LANG-002` governs the page's own wording, not the clinic's data.
+5. The page carries the navigation every page carries (`REQ-SYS-001`), and no navigation entry anywhere points to it.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts) · **ADR:** [ADR: Read-Model Derivation in Value Types](adr/2026-08-24-read-model-derivation-in-value-types.md)
